quran[7]{c,v,t}:
  18,21,"So in this way, We brought them to the people’s attention so that they may know that Allah’s promise (of the Resurrection) is true, and as for the Last Hour, there is no doubt about it. As they (i.e. the town’s people) were disputing among themselves in their matter, they said: ‘Construct a building over them; their Lord knows best about them.’ Those who prevailed over their affair said: ‘We shall build a place of worship over them.’"
  18,22,"Some will say: ‘(The Companions of the Cave) were three, and the fourth of them was their dog.’ And others will say: ‘(They were) five, and the sixth of them was their dog.’ (They are) guessing at the Unseen. Yet others will say: ‘(They were) seven, and the eighth of them was their dog.’ Say: ‘My Lord knows best their number, and none (truly) knows about them except a few.’ So do not dispute concerning them except with a clear argument. And do not question any of them about them."
  18,23,"And do not say of anything: ‘I will surely do it tomorrow,’"
  18,24,except (adding): ‘If Allah wills so.’ And remember your Lord when you forget. And say: ‘Perhaps my Lord will guide me to what is closer to right conduct than this.’
  18,25,"They remained in their cave for three hundred years, adding nine more (to that number).*"
  18,26,Say: ‘Allah knows best how long they stayed.’ To Him belongs the Unseen of the heavens and the earth. How wonderful His seeing and how wonderful His hearing! They have no guardian besides Him. And He does not make anyone a partner in His judgement.
  18,27,Recite what has been revealed to you from your Lord’s Book. None can change His Words. And you will never find any refuge besides Him.
